C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/cxlaunchland_20261016\v5pass\glm_cxlandv5.txt:6:**Change 1 — the redirections' truncation edge is unpinned (floor breach).** [REASONED] `> "$TXT"` → `>> "$TXT"` (and the `2>` twin) passes all 224: every row's out dir is fresh, and D1's second call writes only after the mv renamed the first run's files. The CONTRACT lists "the output names and the stdout/stderr redirections" pinned by N1F, but no row straddles truncate-vs-append. This is not benign: the pack runner re-fires jobs whose log lacks the done phrases [READ U14, KNOWN RESIDUALS], so a production re-run into the same out dir/tag would append a stale run to a new one — `body > 0` with concatenated content can exit 0 and be read as the answer. Fix: one row that runs into a pre-seeded out dir (or twice into the same dir/tag) and applies the N1F byte-compare; add `m_append`/`m_appenderr`.
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/cxlaunchland_20261016\v5pass\glm_cxlandv5.txt:8:**Change 2 — the effort overrides' "honoured" edge is unpinned (floor breach).** [REASONED] `EFFORT="${CX_EFFORT:-ultra}"` → `EFFORT=ultra` passes all 224, as do its twins (`AUP_EFFORT=ultra`; call-site `"$AUP_EFFORT"` → `"$EFFORT"`). [READ] No row sets CX_EFFORT or CX_AUP_EFFORT to anything but empty: EO pins only empty→default (`m_effortcolon`, `m_aupeffcolon`), E1/E2 only the defaults (ultra both). CX_MODEL's honoured edge IS straddled (M1/X5/X13/CH/BA/R7B); the efforts' is the exact hole U10 closed for CX_CODEX_BIN with DP/E0b. Fix: one row with distinct values (e.g. CX_EFFORT=low, CX_AUP_EFFORT=high, refusal+fallback fixture) callseq-compared.
