C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\xscaleinten\panel_20260912_104522_xpadjud\kimi.txt:374:  The inten BIT test (`inten & (1<<22)`): no dominating bit-test predicate exists (l_bit is a plain int parameter tested for truthiness — its "bitness" is in the CALLER, outside the function boundary; the rule says enumerate "to the function boundary"). So bit-test is a fresh shape + fresh constant → clause (e) disclosure ✓. My D1 refinement holds, and it's cleaner than my guess: l_bit inside the function is truthiness, and swapping gives `inten != 0`, which is ALREADY pinned by S1/S2 read rows. So floor cells were: rd==0 (was missing → RD0_ALLONES), and the rest already pinned. 
