C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\xscaleinten\panel_20260912_104522_xpadjud\grok.txt:41:**D1** OVERTURN the lean; the row-add stays. Floor is the dominating predicates (`crm==0` / `crn==0` / `l_bit`) and body-tested partitions of device-state the repair reads. This body **tests nothing**. `rd == k` and `inten & bit` are the `idata == k` shape. I argued that on pass 2; being harder on it: the CONTRACT had already claimed the rd-predicate family at `rd == 15`, so leaving `rd == 0` **undisclosed** was a records hole, not L2. The dispatch-label carve-out is the same answer — a label that reaches the edit and is not re-tested is clause (e). Cheapness is not a discriminator. If you call these floor, the enumeration is 16 rd values × 32 bits × 2³² exact values, which the letter-over-demanded bound already files as (e). **One row per leftover `rd` is the unbounded reading; disclosure-by-construction is the bounded one.** Grade F1/F2 as L1 construction in the CHANGELOG, not L2.
