C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\alphaswpctxreg\pass2_panel_20260908\ollama_kimi.txt:5:**Q1 — by-construction: acceptable, with one re-labeling.** (REASONED) The discrimination table is closed by arithmetic, not measurement, and that is fine: any product state reaches exactly one cell of `(v0, a0)`: correct `(C,N)` green; shipped `(S,C)` red twice; N-repair `(N,N)` red on `v0 ctx`; no-op `(S,N)` red on `v0 ctx`. The distinctness assert in-script makes "wrong repair accidentally hits C" impossible for any repair not returning old-ctx. The executed-path worry (did call 2 even run?) is already extinguished pre-fix by `a0 land = C`, which requires call 2's handler to have fired. **Caveat:** clause (b) — the measured shipped-defect run — and clause (d) cover *different points* in repair space; (d) should stop borrowing (b)'s "measured" weight. A built `v0=N` mutant would add one thing only: cross-validation that the PREFIX/POSTFIX labels weren't swapped. That is calibration, not floor logic. Not owed.
