C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\armmsrmodekill\panel_pass2_20261007\ollama_kimi.txt:12:**4. Floor.** (READ, table) pre-fix 16/26 with exactly the ten named reds, all `dead`, twice. Reinstated exits: `M_load_exit{,_latched}` → `dbg both`; `M_save_exit{,_latched}` → `dbg save, dbg both` — matches. Nulled repairs all red on contract rows. **Un-mutated DEPENDS-ON predicates**: (a) once-suppression (Q3); (b) helper *narrowing* — no mutant rejects a modelled mode (all mutants widen); the disclosed escaping list covers only wrong-yes at unmodelled values, and whether old accept rows drive 0x11/0x12/0x17/0x1b is not visible (old rows not inlined) — settling fact: existence of accept rows for those four modes; (c) arg-edit-vs-mask-edit (disclosed); (d) SPSR-write interception (1. above). Plus the Q1 base-red incident itself: floor demands deterministic base green; two red base runs stand unexplained — counted as the 1 breach.
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\armmsrmodekill\panel_pass2_20261007\ollama_glm.txt:23:READ: pre-fix build fails (HEAD 16/26, all ten reds deaths). Verbatim reinstatement: Save → dbg save + dbg both; Load → dbg both only — correct, since dbg save's Load runs in SVC and dbg both is the only carrier that fires Load's default. Nulled repair: every CONTRACT clause has a confirming mutant (drops: M_drop_msr/pop/dpi; unconditional: M_uncond_*; whole-op: M_wholeop_msr via the if-pin; helper always/wide: M_helper_always1/range; latch sharing: M_shared_* including the probe2 pairings; pop early-return: M_pop_return; DPI announce-gate drop: M_dpi_uncond_call). I re-derived each mutant's red set from the row WANTs; all match the table. READ: DEPENDS-ON predicates un-mutated — yes: (1) the helper's accept side (no mutant narrows it; M_helper_range only widens); (2) the helper's internal `& ARM_FLAG_MODE` (every driven value is < 0x20); (3) the save/load switch case lists (no mutant removes a case; per the packet no row drives a bank switch through 0x11/0x12/0x17/0x1b). (4) decline-bit/backstop-bit sharing is un-mutated but explicitly disclosed — floor-clean by disclosure. Items (1)–(3) are neither mutated nor disclosed: that is the gap.
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\armmsrmodekill\panel_pass2_20261007\ollama_deepseek.txt:31:- REASONED: no DEPENDS-ON predicate appears un-mutated; the table includes mutants for shared decline/backstop bits and unconditional DPI guard.
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\armmsrmodekill\panel_pass2_20261007\grok.txt:45:Un-mutated DEPENDS-ON predicates, the ones the contract already discloses: a helper wrong only at `0x16`, `0x18-0x1a`, `0x1c-0x1d`, or `0x01-0x0f`; a single decline bit aliased with a single backstop bit; a second execution of the same translated MSR. Also un-mutated, and not in that disclosure: the `(mask & ARM_FLAG_MODE)` conjunct alone. Dropping it makes `no cbit` gain `once`, because `f_14`'s `arg[0]` is `0x14` and that row treats any `(once)` as the token. The row would catch it. No mutant was run.
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\xscaleinten\panel_20260912_095235_xscalepass2\ollama_kimi.txt:4:## Q1 — the survivors, and DEPENDS-ON
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\alphaswpctxreg\pass2_panel_20260908\grok.txt:1:I'll inspect the `#514` product, probe, and artifacts in `src/` first, then check the premises those six seats treated as given.Pass-1 panel notes and the actual palcode handler are next, so I can test the floor claim against the tree rather than the write-up.I'll read the pass-1 briefs, witness artifacts, and Alpha PAL docs next, then check whether the wrapper and census claims actually match the tree.Pass-1 seats and the architecture sources are next; I need to see which census and wrapper claims actually got corrected.I'll check the vacuity-floor rule, the `#507` probe, `alphatbinegsel` coupling, and whether `print` can accidentally yield `C`.**VERDICT: The one-identifier product is correct and sufficient. The witness is a real rung-3 red-then-green. The round is not complete as argued: clause (d) was misnamed, `a0 land` pins a value the architecture does not require, and the probe is blind to a hardcoded `v0 = 0x01000000`. None of that is an L2 floor breach. Do not owe a built `v0 = a0` mutant. Do not treat the `alphatbinegsel` re-baseline as a `#514` flush debt — this hunk did not touch the invalidate.**
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\xscaleinten\panel_20260912_095235_xscalepass2\ollama_glm.txt:7:DEPENDS-ON (READ): the site predicates crm==0, crn==0, l_bit are pinned true by every subject read, so mutants keyed on them degenerate to HEAD (killed, 12/29). The free dimensions are the body-read fields `rd` and `i80321_inten`, and the rows cover each only at finitely many points.
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\xscaleinten\panel_20260912_095235_xscalepass2\ollama_glm.txt:13:**Your three candidates:** (1) inten-bit — floor cell, **survives** (above). (2) `rd==0` — floor cell; `rd==0` itself is **not settleable from the packet** (Rd fields of D_OP1/ANCHOR_M1/X4_NOP unstated), but the undriven-rd class survives with certainty. (3) `isteer != 0` — **clause-(e) disclosure**: the crn-0 read body never reads isteer (READ), so it is outside your DEPENDS-ON enumeration; it also survives, since isteer is 0 at every inten read (REASONED: SIB_WRITE dies at its write; IWP zeroes isteer first; no row writes isteer then reads inten). Note the sweep's breadth is inconsistent: isrc, opcode1, opcode2, and a read counter — all equally outside DEPENDS-ON — were built and killed, while `isteer != 0` and a 6th-read counter (D's five reads are the maximum any session drives, READ) were not; both are 29/29 green.
