pair is `goto crime_declined`, bypassing the register switch.  The jump omits the dispatch; that omission does not make the whole repair path empty of reads, writes or tests (it reads and writes the latch).  The added axis consists of the skipped dispatch's GUEST-OBSERVABLE labels.  Cross it with the applicable code-tested predicate and state partitions under the existing bounds: the guard's dominating predicates and the jointly reachable device-state lvalues read by the fix's own repair path, as defined by pass 11 above.  This does not make every test or state in the skipped arms a floor axis; the existing partition, reachability and generating-set bounds still apply.  At `#529` the repair path tests the warning latch, so its CLEAR and SET states belong explicitly in the enumeration.  TIME and REV with the latch SET were the demonstrated holes at repair 14 -- `M3_timelatch` and `M5_revlatch` escaped at 204/204 while `M4_timeplain` was detected at 200/204 and `M6_istlatch` at 201/204 (`repair14_20260916/POSTTABLE.out`) -- and were CLOSED by repair 15 (table 14: 214/218 both; table 16: 222/226 both, `table16_20260926/POSTTABLE16.out`).  Those holes were never the whole enumeration, and detection of the plain TIME variant does not discharge the latch-conditioned variants.  The INTMASK and CONTROL-write label-swaps were measured DETECTED: table 13a `M7_intmasklatch` / `M8_ctllatch` 201/204 each, table 16 223/226 each.  An OFFSET within one label is not an axis unless the body distinguishes it: `#529`'s entry 34 (`sd +0x40`, latch CLEAR) is unrowed while its label cell is held at +0x278 -- the unrowed-slot class, clause (e).  Include only labels whose skipped arms have guest-observable effects.  CRIME's DOG arm is a bare `break;` and its `default:` body is host-debug only, so neither contributes a floor label for THIS skipped-dispatch face.  This exclusion does not establish guest equivalence for ACCEPTED accesses at those labels: CRIME's width arm supplies `+0x0c`'s observable value before `default:` prints.  DISCHARGE requires measured DETECTION by the shipped instrument of each enumerated label-swap variant, including the relevant state-conditioned variants.  Existing rows may discharge them; predictions or aggregate detection do not substitute for the individual measurements.  Table 11's K2 PER-ROW prediction error is the recorded caution.  The added label enumeration is bounded to the ONE skipped dispatch in the enclosing function; it does not recurse into further dispatches or dispatches in callees.  MINTED FROM ONE DEVICE: on first reuse, check that the skipped-label enumeration and its bounded predicate/state product fit the new device.**  And the measuring seat's own bound -- the cross-product
