C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\armmsrmodekill\panel_pass2r4_20261008\codex.txt:1162:GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/armmsrmodekill\panel_pass2r_20261007\codex.txt:2156:GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\crimewidthkill\repair16_f2_20260926\fable5_f2_adjudication.md:38:1. **My pass-2 L2 grade for `H_noresetclear` rests on SIBLING PARITY with a channel-validity ruling, not on a floor clause as written.** The 13/17 conditional made the DOG pair owed because the accepted 0x0200 cell's ONLY observable was the text count; the accepted 0x0800 cells already had a varying channel (the halt, K_ctl4w/8w_reset_post). I extended L2 to the HARD_RESET clear by analogy -- HARD_RESET is a partition the arm TESTS -- and the round accepted it. The repair is right and cheap and no seat disputes it; but the contract must cite that warrant (13/17 + parity over the arm's tested bits) rather than invent a class. And it draws the line for X3 exactly: a TESTED partition earns parity; an UNTESTED conjunct (the latch, bit 0) is clause (e). One step further and it is #392.
