C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\armmsrmodekill\panel_pass2r4_20261008\codex.txt:1314:GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/armmsrmodekill\panel_pass2r3_20261008\codex.txt:4359:GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/armmsrmodekill\opus_pass2_20261007\opus_pass2.md:134:- **The msr_imm guard has NO label axis.** Its body tests only `== USR32`, and that partition is rowed by `usr mask`. An `&& cur == SVC` conjunct there is a value the body never tests as a case, so it is clause (e), disclosable.
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\armmsrmodekill\panel_pass2r4_20261008\codex.txt:1316:GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/armmsrmodekill\panel_pass2r3_20261008\codex.txt:4364:GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/armmsrmodekill\witness_20261007\opus_pass1.md:85:**Scope note the brief omits:** the helper will also refuse modes 0x00-0x0F, the 26-bit hole. The probe docstring (`:59-61`) bans `#0` as a stimulus because "it rows the 26-bit hole, which is a DIFFERENT defect with its own disposition." Today mode 0 also reaches `default: exit(1)`. A helper that declines every non-modelled mode silently disposes of that defect too. That outcome is correct, but the round must CLAIM it (contract, clause (e)) or keep it out.
