C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\agypack_20261013\repair4_spec\grok_repair4_spec.txt:8:The class is the operand-swap axis of every dominating guard: clause (2) of "DEPENDS ON enumerates exactly two things" (`GXEMUL-SEC/tools/CLAUDE.md:1432-1435`), at every state the pre-table's GUARD FIELD vs BODY FIELD row owes (`tools/CLAUDE.md:1724`: fields the predicate reads, fields the guarded body reads, and where the writers differ "the detector owes a state where they DISAGREE"), closed as a class because two consecutive passes each found one cell of it. The repair-chain amendment (`tools/CLAUDE.md:2691-2694`): "WHEN TWO CONSECUTIVE PASSES FIND BREACHES OF ONE CLASS, THE NEXT REPAIR OWES THE CLASS CLOSURE: enumerate the full space from the function's own inputs, close every cell in ONE diff, and write into the CONTRACT which cells are covered and which are deliberately not."
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\agypack_20261013\repair4_spec\grok_repair4_spec.txt:112:**`bepop_ge4`** (`mutants/bepop_ge4.c:1210`, `SCORES.txt:127-128`) and **`lepop_ge4`** (`mutants/lepop_ge4.c:1203`, `SCORES.txt:131-132`). The other endian's `len == 4` test is unchanged. Measuring seat: both pass. Reading seat: the pop/consumed family is disclosed with `n_C6` and `n_E_cons_ge4` (`fable5_r3pass.md:90`). Adversarial grok: an 8-byte read pops 4, and the difference is `odata` plus `warned_inbuf_overread`, because `consumed` is untouched (`grok_adversarial_r3pass.txt:39`). Argon: REAL GAP on an 8-byte read, and a completion-only check stays green (`gemini_web.out:14`, `:16`, `:39`). Code supports Argon and adversarial grok on the mechanism, and the joint sentence on the grade. These tests are not dominators. Widths 1..8 attempt 1, 2, 2, 4, 2, 2, 2, 2 pops (`dev_wdc.c:1232-1235`). Widths 5, 6, 7 and 8 sit in the same bucket as width 2. "A value or combination the body never tests as a case is DISCLOSED under clause (e)" (`tools/CLAUDE.md:1454-1456`). On a 2-byte DATA-IN an 8-byte read still consumes 2 (`dev_wdc.c:1255`, then the clamp at `:1290-1291`), still completes, and differs only in the two extra empty-ring `-1` bytes (`wdc_get_inbuf`, `dev_wdc.c:288-303`) and the overread latch. (e) DISCLOSED. Name both edits in record 3. A row that checks only SECCNT or CYL does not kill them.
