C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\agypack_20261013\changelog_563_draft\grok_changelog_563_draft.txt:20:**Closing pass (2026-10-13) -- the flagship measures one floor breach, so the chain stays open.** Fable 5.1: `BREACH` (`close_20261013/fable5/fable5_close.md:5-10`). The edit is `inbuf_len == 12` changed to `inbuf_len <= 12` at the CDB dispatch, which she anchors at `dev_wdc.c:1717`. Her input: a CDB delivered as six 16-bit words in `PHASE_CMDOUT`; the variant dispatches at word 1. It passes all 150 rows. The row she owes: the compare's below edge, ten queued bytes plus one 1-byte write, want 0 dispatches, in the idiom of `occupancy above 12 does not dispatch`. Her ten runs are `fable5/RESULTS.txt:6-15` (device md5 `71407161`, detector md5 `0f5807b8`, 00:48:12-00:48:26): base 150/0 `WDC_IDENTIFY_PASS`; null `BUILD_FAIL` (485 errors, binary 0); X1 150 rows, 2 failures (both dispatch rows named); P6 150/0 PASS; `VA_dispatch_le12` 150/0 PASS (the breach); `VC_dispatch_eq12_or_11` 150/0 PASS; VD1, VR and VG each 150/0 PASS; VI (`atapi_received += len`) 150 rows, 4 failures. She grades VD1, VR and VG as clause (e), not floor (`fable5_close.md:97-118`). She did not re-run the 193 (`fable5_close.md:126`). Her disposition: this pass finds one floor breach, so the chain stays open; the next repair is one row (occupancy 11), the contract's two-edge line, the records corrections, and the optional L1 fixture change, re-run against the whole table, and that diff owes its own pass 2 (`fable5_close.md:195-198`). She read the clean-clone receipt as `REGRESS_PASS`, 381 checks, 0 FAIL lines, those two md5s, `BINARY_FRESH=yes` (`fable5_close.md:123-124`). Grok adversarial close: a different `BREACH`, `received < data_in_len` widened with `|| data_in_len == 0`, and the same cell as `received <= data_in_len - 1`, "both pass all 150 rows" (`close_20261013/grok_adversarial_close.txt:1-3`); the same file says no table was re-run and the 150-row claims are from the row bodies (`grok_adversarial_close.txt:56`). Panel `panel_20261013_003110/SEAT_VERDICTS.txt:1-11`: 8 answered, 0 walled. agy `BREACH` on P2, `if (!d->io_enabled)` to `if (0)` (`agy.txt:1`); grok `BREACH` on the same P2 edit (`grok.txt:3`); deepseek `BREACH` (delete `relative_addr /= d->addr_mult`) (`ollama_deepseek.txt:1`); minimax `BREACH` (delete the `#475` consumed clamp) (`ollama_minimax.txt:1`); glm `NOT CHECKABLE` (`ollama_glm.txt:1`); ollama_kimi `NOT CHECKABLE` (`ollama_kimi.txt:1`); kimi 284 bytes, no verdict line (`SEAT_VERDICTS.txt:5`). P2's clean sweep was already measured on REPAIR2: `if (!io_enabled)` to `if (0)` passes every row, guest consequence reasoned, not measured on a guest (`SUMMARY2.txt:44-49`). The flagship lists that same P2 inside "zero further breaches" as disclosed and not rowed (`fable5_close.md:73-75`). Astra had already graded it floor (`codex_astra_confirm_v2.txt:32`).
