C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\agypack_20261013\carrier_d2_texts\grok_carrier_d2_texts.txt:131:**AND THE JOIN ITSELF, adjudicated 2026-09-09 on `sgimtedepth4dead` 7g-1 after a MEASURED total escape: a dispatch LABEL is a floor axis of an edited guard when the selector's value FLOWS INTO an lvalue the guarded body reads or writes within the enclosing function (there, `dst_mode = (dst_tlb << 10) + ...` two lines above a repair of `dst_mode |= RGBA`), or when the body re-tests it after the join (TxICR); a label that reaches the edit and touches nothing the body reads is clause (e) (the `mode & COPY` shape).  A detector rowing one label of three was swept 14/14 by `&& dst_tlb == MTE_TLB_A` while a guest-only control showed the closed defect live at the other two (`regress/artifacts/sgimtedepth4dead/killtable3_20260909/`).  The floor it adds is {labels} x the guard operand's body-tested partition -- six cells there, two rows owed -- never the labels' cross-product with everything.**
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\agypack_20261013\carrier_d2_texts\grok_carrier_d2_texts.txt:134:The next bold on the same line is the third disjunct, from `**AND A GUARD THAT SUPPRESSES A DISPATCH ADDS A THIRD DISJUNCT TO THE 2026-09-09 LABEL CLAUSE` through `fit the new device.**`. Neither one-sentence addition rewrites it. Its opening rule is: a dispatch LABEL is also a floor axis when the edited guard's repair bypasses that dispatch in the enclosing function, and absence of data flow into the body or of a re-test after the join does not put a qualifying suppression label in clause (e) (`CLAUDE.md:1487`).
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\agypack_20261013\carrier_d2_texts\grok_carrier_d2_texts.txt:136:FLAG: `CLAUDE.md:1432-1435` makes every predicate that dominates the edited lines, walked up to the enclosing function, a floor axis. `CLAUDE.md:1487` makes a label whose body reads nothing of the selector clause (e). Nothing in either sentence says whether a binary result-`if` is a label or a dominating predicate. Reading 1 grades that `if` clause (e). Reading 2 leaves the DEPENDS-ON bound in force. `fable5_records_adjudication.md:145` records that split; `regress/artifacts/wdc473floor/f2_20261009/fable5/fable5_ruling_v2.md:62-69` is the `res == 1` case it came from.
