C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\agypack_20261013\carrier_d2_texts\agy_carrier_d2_texts.txt:162:> before its table ran (Opus, pass 10).  **AND THE JOIN ITSELF, adjudicated 2026-09-09 on `sgimtedepth4dead` 7g-1 after a MEASURED total escape: a dispatch LABEL is a floor axis of an edited guard when the selector's value FLOWS INTO an lvalue the guarded body reads or writes within the enclosing function (there, `dst_mode = (dst_tlb << 10) + ...` two lines above a repair of `dst_mode |= RGBA`), or when the body re-tests it after the join (TxICR); a label that reaches the edit and touches nothing the body reads is clause (e) (the `mode & COPY` shape).  A detector rowing one label of three was swept 14/14 by `&& dst_tlb == MTE_TLB_A` while a guest-only control showed the closed defect live at the other two (`regress/artifacts/sgimtedepth4dead/killtable3_20260909/`).  The floor it adds is {labels} x the guard operand's body-tested partition -- six cells there, two rows owed -- never the labels' cross-product with everything.**  And the measuring seat's own bound -- the cross-product
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\agypack_20261013\carrier_d2_texts\agy_carrier_d2_texts.txt:168:**AND A GUARD THAT SUPPRESSES A DISPATCH ADDS A THIRD DISJUNCT TO THE 2026-09-09 LABEL CLAUSE, adjudicated 2026-09-25 on `#529` by the flagship's first-hand Q3 re-ruling, with GPT-6 Astra's amendments of 2026-09-26 (`crimewidthkill/rerule_20260925/`); this text is the codex seat's 2026-09-26 rewrite of the clause (`codexfarm_20260926/codex_carrierq3.txt`, "faithful with changes"), adopted with three corrections by the flagship's final ruling of 2026-09-30 (`crimewidthkill/final529r18_20260926/fable5_final.md`, item E): a dispatch LABEL is ALSO a floor axis when the edited guard's repair bypasses that dispatch in the enclosing function.  This is an alternative to selector data flow into the guarded body or re-testing after the join; absence of those two connections does not put a qualifying suppression label in clause (e).  At CRIME the repair is `goto crime_declined`, bypassing the register switch.  The jump omits the dispatch; that omission does not make the whole repair path empty of reads, writes or tests (it reads and writes the latch).  The added axis consists of the skipped dispatch's GUEST-OBSERVABLE labels.  Cross it with the applicable code-tested predicate and state partitions under the existing bounds: the guard's dominating predicates and the jointly reachable device-state lvalues read by the fix's own repair path, as defined by pass 11 above.  This does not make every test or state in the skipped arms a floor axis; the existing partition, reachability and generating-set bounds still apply.  At `#529` the repair path tests the warning latch, so its CLEAR and SET states belong explicitly in the enumeration.  TIME and REV with the latch SET were the demonstrated holes at repair 14 -- `M3_timelatch` and `M5_revlatch` escaped at 204/204 while `M4_timeplain` was detected at 200/204 and `M6_istlatch` at 201/204 (`repair14_20260916/POSTTABLE.out`) -- and were CLOSED by repair 15 (table 14: 214/218 both; table 16: 222/226 both, `table16_20260926/POSTTABLE16.out`).  Those holes were never the whole enumeration, and detection of the plain TIME variant does not discharge the latch-conditioned variants.  The INTMASK and CONTROL-write label-swaps were measured DETECTED: table 13a `M7_intmasklatch` / `M8_ctllatch` 201/204 each, table 16 223/226 each.  An OFFSET within one label is not an axis unless the body distinguishes it: `#529`'s entry 34 (`sd +0x40`, latch CLEAR) is unrowed while its label cell is held at +0x278 -- the unrowed-slot class, clause (e).  Include only labels whose skipped arms have guest-observable effects.  CRIME's DOG arm is a bare `break;` and its `default:` body is host-debug only, so neither contributes a floor label for THIS skipped-dispatch face.  This exclusion does not establish guest equivalence for ACCEPTED accesses at those labels: CRIME's width arm supplies `+0x0c`'s observable value before `default:` prints.  DISCHARGE requires measured DETECTION by the shipped instrument of each enumerated label-swap variant, including the relevant state-conditioned variants.  Existing rows may discharge them; predictions or aggregate detection do not substitute for the individual measurements.  Table 11's K2 PER-ROW prediction error is the recorded caution.  The added label enumeration is bounded to the ONE skipped dispatch in the enclosing function; it does not recurse into further dispatches or dispatches in callees.  MINTED FROM ONE DEVICE: on first reuse, check that the skipped-label enumeration and its bounded predicate/state product fit the new device.**
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\agypack_20261013\carrier_d2_texts\agy_carrier_d2_texts.txt:175:A binary result-`if` whose guarded body never reads the selector is a dispatch label for this check, placing its unread selector cells in clause (e) debt rather than on the floor.
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\wdcidselfcheck_20260925\pass551d\fable5_pass551d.md:47:Wrong: G2 (overturned). Incomplete: G5 (the conditional form) and G1 (the trailer unnamed as a class). Missed by everyone including me until this reading: (1) the trailer class cannot be closed in-file, which is why every in-file "closure" moved the composite one site — the contract, not another repair, is the honest form, and the lane is the close; (2) the conditional both-tally reset is green AT THE TRAILER — the dedicated grok named it in passing and no disclosure sentence carried it; (3) a valid zero's denominator belongs in the CONTRACT, not only in the pass record, so Astra's and later escapes are classified against clause (e) instead of re-litigated as breaches. One caution: the "not closable in-file" claim is reasoned from the single-call-site argument, not measured; a seat that shows an in-file pin on `main()`'s trailer that survives one inlining edit and one inserted conditional reset would overturn it, and #551e's pass should be asked exactly that.
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\fablequeue8n_20261009\astra_confirm\codex_astra_n6pcc2.txt:21:   The deciding rules are **“DEPENDS ON enumerates exactly two things”** and the derived-input rule: dominating predicates and guarded-body reads/tests bound the enumeration. X’s newly introduced read cannot enlarge the original body’s closure. “One-token perversion,” the same undesirable consequence, and a finite two-case domain do not override those bounds. [DEPENDS-ON bound](C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/CLAUDE.md:1432), [derived-input rule](C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/CLAUDE.md:1598)
