C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\agypack_20261013\adj_563_ruling\grok_adj_563_ruling.txt:75:Ruling sentences that match the pinned text: prong 2 is operand-swap candidates for a guard, not a floor over every body-read field (`fable5_ruling_v2.md:75-76`, rules `:1364-1365`) TRUE. Sibling parity is a row or a sentence, so the phase channel is not a floor class (`fable5_ruling_v2.md:58-61`) TRUE. Absence-record rule does not demand the second-transfer row (`fable5_ruling_v2.md:79-83`, rules `:2332-2333`) TRUE. Repair-chain close conditions in ruling §4 (`:133-148`) match `:2424-2428`, `:2440-2442`, and `:2446-2448`. "DEPENDS-ON off write targets" (`fable5_ruling_v2.md:38-39`) is in neither CLAUDE.md.
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\agypack_20261013\adj_563_ruling\grok_adj_563_ruling.txt:79:They do not disagree on the phase channel. Ruling `:57-61` grades the phase the arm and the re-arm leave LICENSED, not floor, because it is an assignment and sibling parity allows a row or a sentence. Confirmation `:13` says the same: "Licensed, not floor." Pinned `tools/CLAUDE.md:1593` supports that shared sentence. The confirmation adds that the 1-left row also carries the remainder predicate. The ruling already puts `received < data_in_len` and its B−1 edge on the closure list (`fable5_ruling_v2.md:112-114`). `REPAIR2.c.txt:1008-1012` and `:6295-6299` attach that edge to the same 1-left row and say D2's letter is for a constant bound, so this compare is held under DEPENDS-ON. That is a second job of one row, not a conflict on the phase grade. Parent D2 (`CLAUDE.md:1541-1548`) would not make the phase assignment floor: it applies to `X > B` / `e < 96`.
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\agypack_20261013\adj_563_ruling\grok_adj_563_ruling.txt:81:P2 `io_enabled`. The ruling never names P2 or `io_enabled`. Its D3 holding (`fable5_ruling_v2.md:62-68`) is only `res == 1` as clause (e), because `res` is a three-way result selector the push body does not read, and `data_in != NULL` as floor. Confirmation `:32` grades P2 Floor: a function-level enable guard over both edited sites, not a dispatch label, and says REPAIR2's blanket (e) for P1/P2/P6 is wrong for P2. Pinned DEPENDS ON (`:1362-1365`, floor at `:1431-1436`) counts `!io_enabled` (`dev_wdc.c:1176`) as a predicate dominating both #473 sites inside `DEVICE_ACCESS`. The label clause (`:1417`) gives clause (e) to a dispatch label that touches nothing the body reads. `io_enabled` is not that label. The quoted pinned text supports the confirmation's Floor sentence. It supports the ruling's (e) sentence for `res == 1` / `res == 0` (P6), not for `io_enabled`. "Under the ruling's own D3 reading" is the confirmation's application; the ruling text does not contain it.
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\agypack_20261013\adj_563_ruling\grok_adj_563_ruling.txt:91:- "Every dispatch arm" irq-checked. Ruling `:146-147` tells the closing pass to verify that. Confirmation `:46` says `res == 0` is still unrowed, so it is not established. Product `:1765-1776` and `PRETABLE2.out:35-37` support the confirmation. The repair-chain amendment (`tools/CLAUDE.md:2461-2464`) supports writing the reject arm into the contract as covered or excluded; it does not say repetition turns an unconditional store into a DEPENDS-ON predicate. The ruling already called the irq check not DEPENDS-ON floor (`fable5_ruling_v2.md:38-40`).
