seat failure. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260905_112529</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">N/A</span><span class="tip">2026-09-05 — CONFIRMED — FILE-READING (grok-4.6 xhigh, --prompt-file; 13 KB; verified against the live tree -- default arm at 664-703 -- and opened BASE and nine mutant .out files).  YES, close: a valid pass, repair diff inlined, roster named, zero floor breaches with a denominator.  Encoders match cpu_m88k_instr.c and the width probe; the srvd register plan re-derived instruction by instruction (big-endian memcpy of the T1CMP word store; `srvd wr latch&#x27; 0x78 is not a guess -- BASE 46/46 and M_BACKEDLOW&#x27;s 0xbb/0xbb78 discriminator show the store landing when it does); text anchors do not collide (read format `-- served 0x%02x&#x27;, write format `: 0x%x -- declined&#x27;; the len-2 write is silent).  All 22 die for the claimed reason with one honest accident named: M_LATCHRD0&#x27;s extra `half wr rdawr&#x27; 0x78 is the second ld.hu&#x27;s zeroed data[0] (0x0078), the same family as the unlatch extras; the len-2 re-kill&#x27;s FATE pin is batch-level (a `len==2 &amp;&amp; MEM_WRITE&#x27; re-kill is indistinguishable from the READ one on this session -- channel coarseness, not a floor hole; do not split the session).  MIRROR table for the ten rows: the write-announce value/label at len 2 is NEITHER (the st.h is silent) -- a CLAIM-row gap since `len&#x27; is no `if&#x27; in the arm, so the filter must not demand a row; the len-4 byte-selection cell is UNROWABLE (word-aligned uncased windows hold zeros; ld.w at 0x04 is cased and at 0x05 is rejected before memory_rw); the in-word/unnamed READ counts are NEITHER (covered at 0x05 when unlatched) and the first-access len-2 write is equivalent to identity today.  M_BACKEDLOW&#x27;s mirror (member 6 for ra &gt;= 0x14) already reds the pass-2 rows -- the in-word pair was a missing CLASS, not a missing polarity.  Smallest 46/46 edits: M_RELOAD (measured), len 8, single-offset member 6 or latch skip, write value 0 only at len 2 -- all in or added to the exclusions; no DEPENDS-ON operand swap or guard weakening green on 46 found.  TWO L4s, both corrected: the contract cited &#x27;Opus M_RELOAD, MEASURED 44/44&#x27; -- there was never a 44-row probe (36 -&gt; 46; table 4 says 46/46 and 36/36); the &#x27;announce COUNT likewise (a silent skip of one unsampled offset passes)&#x27; sentence went stale when every offset of every class gained a counted write (true now only of READ counts outside the named class).  Denominator phrase &#x27;five channels on both arms&#x27; loosened to the widths actually announced (write value at 1 and 4, read value at 1 and 2, width label at 1/2/4 on reads and 1/4 on writes).  `half wr rdawr&#x27; pins the DISPOSITION of a latched st.h, not the write text -- named, not counted as a write-value row. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260905_112529</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">N/A</span><span class="tip">2026-09-05 — CONFIRMED — FILE-READING (kimi CLI, kimi-code/k3; the 108 KB pointer form paged fine; 326 KB of transcript ending in a formatted review and a verdict line -- unlike pass 3).  NO-GO.  It BUILT in its own scratch clone (/tmp/p4_seat_501) and MEASURED M_WRLEN2SILENT -- the write announce suppressed at len == 2 with the latch still set -- at 46/46, twice, a differential proof of the same cell every other seat named: the len-2 WRITE announce is never observed because the probe&#x27;s one st.h is latch-silenced.  It grades the cell clause (d) and NO-GO; adjudicated clause (e) (len is printed, never tested by the arm -- the joint-cells rule enumerates only body-tested partitions; the Opus, grok and Fable seats read it the same way) -&gt; DISCLOSED with its one-instruction repair spec, filed pcc2anngrid.  Q1: encoders, register plan, alignment, anchors and `srvd wr latch&#x27; 0x78 verified.  Q2: the 22 kills causal, the five safe misses understood as double-duty rows, not accidents.  Q3 mirrors: nine of ten rowed or disclosed; the tenth is the cell above; len-4 byte selection indistinguishable by construction.  RECORDS: the 44/44 (corrected), the PANEL501P4-OWED placeholder (defanged here; this pass&#x27;s own marker, filled by this record), the &#x27;both ways&#x27; denominator wording (narrowed to the widths actually announced).  Something else: the literal `(once)&#x27; marker is pinned by no row -- dropping it passes 46 (cosmetic; the latch behaviour is pinned by the count rows) -&gt; disclosed.  Independently recomputed the 43-offset partition, all md5s, the PRETABLE/driver.log order, the gate arithmetic 857 + 10 = 867. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260905_112529</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">N/A</span><span class="tip">2026-09-05 — BELIEVED — PACKET-FED (glm-5.3:cloud; answered the 14.8 KB lean packet, 3.8 KB, no burn).  Q1 READ: the five discrepancies are all safe-direction, cross-checked row by row against the red sets; no predicted red stayed green.  Q2 REASONED from the measured red sets: two mirror cells NEITHER rowed nor disclosed -- the len-2 WRITE announce text (the detector&#x27;s only len-2 store is latch-silenced, so the cell is never exercised; M_WRVAL0 reddens only the len-1 and len-4 write texts) and the len-4 READ announce value (M_SRVD0 reddens no wide row; the served byte there is 0).  Verdict DO NOT CLOSE YET pending a row per cell or an explicit disclosure; it named the fact that settles it (&#x27;grep the width rows for a len-2 declined text or len-4 served text count&#x27;) and could not settle from the packet whether `unnamed rdawr&#x27; was new (ten vs eleven `+row(&#x27; lines -- the eleventh is the reworded `srvd val text&#x27;).  ADJUDICATED: both cells are len-scoped single-operand marginals (len is printed, never tested by the arm) -&gt; DISCLOSED in the contract, not rowed (the same ruling as grok