d class); ONE content row, `alias msg&#x27;, has no non-lethal kill in any table -- the fold mutant is FILED (pcc2anngrid), LOW, outside the fix&#x27;s diff.  `genctl rt&#x27;/`t1cmp word rt&#x27; are BASE-anchored negative controls (said so in the contract now).  Every contract line maps to a measured non-lethal kill except the fold line; disclosed == measured escapes.  Hygiene verified: clone cmp-clean + sentinel cleared after a rebuild; nothing written to any project tree.  Artifacts: measure.sh/.log, verify.sh, FABLE_BASE.out, FABLE_MEXIT.out beside FINDINGS.md. — evidence: regress/artifacts/pcc2defaultkill/regress_20260905/FINDINGS.md</span></span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-closed"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">lunaabsentcpu</span><span class="ttl">lunaabsentcpu  dev_luna88k.c reassert_interrupts() calls the NULL interrupt callback of an UNCONFIGURED cpu slot: on the default one-cpu luna-88k two ordinary guest word stores (INT_ST_MASK1 then SOFT_INT1) kill the emulator process with SIGSEGV -- MEASURED, rung 3</span><span class="tip">lunaabsentcpu  dev_luna88k.c reassert_interrupts() calls the NULL interrupt callback of an UNCONFIGURED cpu slot: on the default one-cpu luna-88k two ordinary guest word stores (INT_ST_MASK1 then SOFT_INT1) kill the emulator process with SIGSEGV -- MEASURED, rung 3 — commits: 79cd12e — witness: probe:regress/luna_absentcpu_probe.py -- a guest store of 0xfc000000 to INT_ST_MASK1 followed by a store to SOFT_INT1 killed the emulator with SIGSEGV on the default one-cpu machine; measured pre-fix, green post-fix — note: 
