</span><span class="ttl">dev_mk48txx.c: EIGHT offsets inside the device&#x27;s own mapped range (0x1ff0-0x1ff7) fall to a default: arm that calls exit(1), so an ordinary guest read of the MK48T08 clock page ends the emulator process -- and machine_mvme88k.c attaches the device unconditionally</span><sup class="b b-A">A</sup><span class="tip">dev_mk48txx.c: EIGHT offsets inside the device&#x27;s own mapped range (0x1ff0-0x1ff7) fall to a default: arm that calls exit(1), so an ordinary guest read of the MK48T08 clock page ends the emulator process -- and machine_mvme88k.c attaches the device unconditionally — FIXED AND SHIPPED AS #521.  Eight ordinary NVRAM bytes inside the device&#x27;s own 8192-byte registration fell to a default: arm that calls exit(1); the accept block&#x27;s lower bound was one term short.  ONE TOKEN fixes it, and it is a BOUNDARY CORRECTION rather than new policy because the backing storage already existed.  Witnessed at rung 3 BEFORE the edit (15/47 -&gt; 46/47) with a conjunction oracle -- wait status AND a post-access observable -- so death, a hang and a fatal() that merely prints are three distinguishable states, which matters because this fork&#x27;s fatal() does not exit.  TWO measured corrections to the filing: the population is SIXTEEN cells not eight, and the kill is WIDTH-INDEPENDENT so there is no width axis to close.  THE DETECTOR TOOK TWO REPAIRS, both of the SAME CLASS: table 1 found the survive-only hole at the control register (M_ICSR escaped 47/47 because the mutated condition is a tautology and the rows there assert only that the access completed), and pass 2 found it again on the eight accepted bytes.  Two consecutive findings triggered the class closure -- nine round-trip rows in one diff, each writing a distinct byte.  AND PASS 2 CAUGHT AN APPARATUS DEFECT IN THE ROUND&#x27;S OWN TABLE: M_NULL replaced a statement with a COMMENT, which is whitespace, so `goto ret&#x27; became the if-body and the leg measured a different mutant while the record claimed clause (d) was satisfied; rebuilt braced, and t3 measures exactly what was claimed.  Floor clause (b) is unsatisfiable literally -- this diff removes no kill, it makes one unreachable -- and the round says so and substitutes M_OLD rather than pretending.  SEATS: the fix ratified by every seat expressing a view; fable5 WALLED with no substitute, re-fired once, named; kimi CLI walled and COVERED by its cloud substitute; agy deliberately not fired.  One BREACH verdict REFUTED with its warrant (the rows it said were missing exist). — witness: probe:regress/artifacts/mk48nvramkill/opus_mk48_nvram_witness_20260910.py -- RUNG 3 on unmodified `-E mvme88k -e mvme187&#x27;, real MC88100 instructions through real decode and real memory_rw, nothing added to reach the site.  MEASURED BEFORE THE EDIT: 15/47 (opus_witness_run_20260910.txt), all 15 controls green and all 32 kill rows red.  AFTER: 46/47 (postfix_run_20260910.txt), every kill row green and every control held.  SHIPPED DETECTOR: regress/mk48_nvram_probe.py, 57 rows, killtable_20260910/t3/SCORES.txt -- BASE 57/57, null medium 16/57, five mutants 16..56/57, ZERO ESCAPES, restore verified on both parts.</span></span><span class="state st-closed">closed</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-closed"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-closed"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><spa