ut 0 -- one of the most common 64-bit PowerPC instructions returns 0 for every input — FIXED AND SHIPPED AS #522.  X(rldicl) wrote ZERO to its destination on every execution: the mask was ORed into the ROTATED VALUE while the destination got `tmp &amp; tmp2&#x27; and tmp2 was never anything but 0.  ONE TOKEN fixes it, and it repairs both halves because the `|=&#x27; had also destroyed the rotated data.  This is the canonical 64-bit masking and zero-extension instruction, so it was wrong on the ordinary path for ordinary compiler output.  WITNESSED at rung 3 before the edit, 19/27 -&gt; 24/27, with a 190-cell census in which every cell was wrong and every cell returned exactly zero.  *** PASS 2 RETURNED BREACH-FOUND WITH TWO MEASURED TOTAL ESCAPES, both repaired in-round: a shift-decode mutant the instrument was blind to BY CONSTRUCTION (the census uses an all-ones source, so rotating it is the identity, and the only rotate-sensitive rows drove shifts below 32 while every logical right shift uses 32 or more); and a condition-register mutant that is NOT INVENTED -- it is the token the sibling handler ships correctly ten lines below. ***  Three rows close both, each the sole killer of its mutant, all three also reddening under the defect and the null medium.  FIVE RECORDS were wrong and are corrected, including a citation in PRODUCT CODE and a detector row that cannot fail under any mutation.  The apparatus failed twice and both failures are preserved rather than deleted -- one of them looked HALF-HEALTHY because two mutators share a mutant name.  Two sibling defects in the same family are filed, measured and unfixed; a gate claim of mine was false and is corrected in place. — witness: probe:regress/artifacts/ppcrldiclzero/opus_ppc_rldicl_witness_20260910.py -- RUNG 3 on unmodified -E bareppc (and testppc, and macppc -e g5), real instructions through real decode and execution, nothing edited to reach the site.  COMMITTED 19/27 with 190 of 190 census cells wrong and all