C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\fbctrlportkill_20260924\panels\panel_20260925_201529\grok.txt:19:The body's own test is one relational operator, `idata >= 8`. There is no `idata & bit` in the port arm. The flagship's generating set for that operator is below, at, and past the bound. Those three are held with the latch clear and with it set: 8 is the first refusal of P, W, and B; values past 8 are the first refusals of F, V, X, Y, and Z; accepts before any refusal are A and W; later accepts are V's fills and Z's selections; later 8s are W's `sh`/`sd` and V's trailing 8. Session B is the one-axis marginal of the 61 bits, which the contract claimed and v5 had left empty. Crossing that marginal with the latch is the two-axis joint (0) already discloses. Multi-axis idata joints stay clause (e). Fifty-eight new processes are the expansion the 2026-09-04 bound was written to stop.
