C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\fbctrlportkill_20260924\panels\panel_20260924_115517\codex.txt:5860:GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\mapledmaaddr\panel_20260912_131634_maplepass2\brief_sent.md:41:  survival + exit status.  Value-keyed exits (`d->dmaaddr == v`, `& bit`) are clause (e), taken as L1 rows because cheap.
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\fbctrlportkill_20260924\panels\panel_20260924_115517\codex.txt:6286:GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\mapledmaaddr\fable_pass2_20260912.md:22:**D1 — UPHOLD (e) / rows L1, and CORRECT THE REASON in the header.** Two different not-floor reasons were written as one. `} else if (d->dmaaddr & 0x1f)` keys on the body-read field — it is INSIDE DEPENDS-ON clause (2) — and is not floor because the body induces no partition of that field (joint-cells rule: *"a value or combination the body never tests as a case ... is DISCLOSED under clause (e)"*; the bounded form: *"the bits of the single value ... are single-operand MARGINALS, not floor"*). `!d->enable`, the static counter and `len` are OUTSIDE the enumeration (not body-read lvalues; `len` is the tail's argument). Opus's `if (X) -> if (X && Y)` shape argument is refuted by its own consequence: it makes `M_BIT30`, `M_EQ4` and `M_ZEROEXIT` floor too and kills the pass-1 and xscaleinten rules (grok). Grading by the consumer's tests is the transitive chasing the bound forbids. The shipped header's sentence *"the consumer-keyed forms (`enable`, the alignment bits, the read count) are outside the BOUND"* is an L4 wrong record on the alignment half — `d->dmaaddr` IS what the body reads. One-line fix.
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\fbctrlportkill_20260924\panels\panel_20260924_115517\codex.txt:6351:GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\mapledmaaddr\fable_pass1_20260912.md:9:**VERDICT: ACCEPT upheld, 9/9 by argument as well as by count. The FAULT member is UNAVAILABLE on SH4 and its idiom is a silent load-skip — that goes into the CHANGELOG *and* corrects the carrier's member-5 clause. Floor = (a)(b)(c) + the accept cell with a POISONED destination + silence over the whole read interval + `other read` (the dominating-predicate complement); everything keyed on a `dmaaddr` value — zero, `== 0x04`, all-ones, the read-to-clear double read — is clause (e), taken as L1 because cheap, never graded floor. The DMA leg is NOT floor: it kills only a new lvalue outside the BOUND; defer it to `mapledmaadvance` with a no-row sentence, or if shipped here, L1 with the refusal-message `E` as its only admissible oracle. The agy witness is ADMISSIBLE as the rung-3 test-first witness (4/12 → 12/12, same script, both controls), but its `read quiet` row is CHANNEL-invalid and must not be carried into the detector unchanged.** Evidence basis: 7/7 scriptable seats, Opus, and agy (fired for measurement, not reading). I read the tree; built nothing.
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\fbctrlportkill_20260924\panels\panel_20260924_115517\codex.txt:6355:GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\mapledmaaddr\fable_pass1_20260912.md:13:**Q2 — row list, under my xscaleinten Q1 rule** (*"the floor is clause (b) verbatim reinstatement plus the dominating predicates' accept cell; every re-introduction keyed on a body-read operand the body does not test (`rd == k`, `field & bit`, `field == v`) is clause (e), disclosed BY CLASS; any row added for one is L1 — licensed because cheap, never graded floor because cheap"*). The body `odata = d->dmaaddr;` tests nothing; dominating predicates `relative_addr == 0x04`, `writeflag != MEM_WRITE`.
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\fbctrlportkill_20260924\panels\panel_20260924_115517\codex.txt:6358:GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\mapledmaaddr\fable_pass1_20260912.md-16-- **`other read` `R(0x10)==0` (the hoist): FLOOR.** The hoist deletes the dominating predicate `relative_addr == 0x04` from the assignment — clause (d) in its purest form, a predicate weakened to `true`. The JOIN ruling does not apply (`relative_addr` flows into nothing the body reads), but the complement cell of a dominating predicate is inside the cross-product. Both prior designs had it; the brief dropped it.
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\fbctrlportkill_20260924\panels\panel_20260924_115517\codex.txt:6359:GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\mapledmaaddr\fable_pass1_20260912.md:17:- **Double read, no write between (glm, Opus): clause (e), L1.** Read-to-clear ADDS a store to a state lvalue; it is neither a predicate weakening nor an operand swap. One extra load — take it, and the contract states "reads have no side effect".
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\fbctrlportkill_20260924\panels\panel_20260924_115517\codex.txt:6361:GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\mapledmaaddr\fable_pass1_20260912.md:19:- **codex's `d->dmaaddr == 0x04`: clause (e), the `idata == k` shape — NOT floor.** This is `rd == 0` with the constant inherited from `relative_addr == 0x04` by coincidence, exactly the reading I overturned this morning: *"floor membership [would] depend on which constant the sibling dispatch happened to carry."* `d->dmaaddr` is a state lvalue, which `rd` was not — but the body tests no partition of it, so its partition is one class and `== 0x04` is `field == v` by the rule's own text. Codex's "reuses existing constants, not arbitrary sweeps" is the coincidence argument restated. A value-4 row costs one write; take it as L1 if wanted; disclose `== k` by class.
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\fbctrlportkill_20260924\panels\panel_20260924_115517\codex.txt:6363:GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\mapledmaaddr\fable_pass1_20260912.md:21:**Q3 — DMA leg: not floor; deferred, or L1 with a stated oracle.** glm/deepseek/ollama-kimi argue "only leg that kills the shadow" — that grades by mutant, not by enumeration. The shadow requires a new lvalue the body does not read; DEPENDS-ON clause (2) draws swaps *"ONLY from fields the guarded BODY reads"*, and the enumeration is diff-closed precisely so a plausible wrong fix outside it is coverage debt, not breach (this is #447's escapes, not #448's). Opus and codex are right on the rule. kimi CLI is right on mechanism and it decides the disposition: an expected value from the read under test is circular; `P+12` certifies the cursor arithmetic `mapledmaadvance` exists to question; the only admissible oracle is the refusal message printing `addr` copied from `d->dmaaddr` at `:382` — an observation of the FIELD, not of the arithmetic — with DEVINFO signatures in verified pre-filled buffers as transfer evidence and `E2 != E1`. **Ruling:** the brief's "recorded consequence" sentence (*"including a post-DMA cursor"*) is a CLAIM→ROW trigger; write the explicit no-row sentence and ship the leg with the cursor row, whose observation channel is this very read arm — load-bearing there, and buildable only after this fix lands. If the round ships it anyway, it is L1 under the RETRY spec verbatim; never a floor claim.
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\fbctrlportkill_20260924\panels\panel_20260924_115517\codex.txt:6371:GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\mapledmaaddr\fable_close_20260912.md:54:- **(b) atexit / time-axis** — split, and the split is the point: the HOST-process-exit `atexit` announce (`M_ATEXIT`, 36/37) is a FLOOR breach (a diagnostic shape, now in-window because the transcript reads through EOF), caught, **L1**; the EMULATED-time-beyond-span periodic report (`M_TICKPERIODIC4`, 37/37) is **clause (e), DISCLOSED window** — correctly NOT floor, and it MUST survive (a kill would mean the window is narrower than stated and the record wrong).
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\fbctrlportkill_20260924\panels\panel_20260924_115517\codex.txt:6400:GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\lcaisalane\opus_c3_20260914\OPUS_ANSWER.md-130-* It is not a DEPENDS-ON (d) breach of the fix: the fix did not touch the `return`.
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\fbctrlportkill_20260924\panels\panel_20260924_115517\codex.txt:6520:GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\m88kexcdeliver\brief_m88kexc_p8.md-27-  a body-read lvalue -- clause (d) floor, unlike the switch-1 arms.  Every SFRZ-set row reached it with IND set and C clear (0x8000000b
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\fbctrlportkill_20260924\panels\panel_20260924_115517\codex.txt:6595:GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\m88kexcdeliver\opus_p2.md:30:**(1) M_NOVBR — L2, floor breach, repair in-round.** `cr[VBR]` is a field the guarded body reads on the delivery path the seven added labels route through, so it is squarely inside the clause-(d) DEPENDS-ON closure, and dropping it is the canonical *keep the guard, null the repair* form: all seven `implemented = true` and all seven tail labels survive textually and the exception lands at the wrong address. **The probe never writes VBR** (`grep -i vbr` on the frozen probe: one docstring mention, no `stcr cr7`), so VBR is 0 in all twelve rows and `cr[VBR] + 8*vector` is arithmetically indistinguishable from `8*vector`. Guest effect: OpenBSD/mvme88k relocates its vector table, so every one of these seven exceptions would enter at the wrong address on the very guest the fix exists to serve. It is compounded by an **L4 wrong record in two places**: the fallback comment says *"DELIVERED (**VBR** + 8\*vector …)"*, and the probe's clause-(e) contract lists *"a wrong vector base"* among what it **catches** — M_VEC4 and M_VEC7 pin the *scaling*, nothing pins the *base register*.
