C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\fbctrlportkill_20260924\panels\panel_20260924_115517\codex.txt:7713:GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\pcc2widthkills\pass11_seats_20260904\fable\FINDINGS.md-51-  R3 (minimax, per-lvalue letter): right that minimax read the OLD contract wording, not clause (d).
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\fbctrlportkill_20260924\panels\panel_20260924_115517\codex.txt:7774:GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\pcc2widthkills\pass10_seats_20260904\fable\FINDINGS.md:46:> *Clause (d)'s DEPENDS-ON closure includes a JOINT cell over two or more of {the guard's operands, the lvalues the guarded body reads} exactly when the guarded body's OWN CODE distinguishes that cell — it tests each lvalue at the partition the cell fixes (e.g. `pending > 0`) and reads them together in one statement or semantic operation. The enumerated cells are the CROSS-PRODUCT of those per-lvalue body-tested partitions — never arbitrary boolean functions of the read-set — and a mutant exempting any single cell whose reachability is MEASURED is a floor breach. Close the whole cross-product in ONE diff and state in the contract which cells are rowed and which disclosed. A value or bit-combination the body never tests as a case (`idata == k`; a byte no conditional distinguishes) is disclosed under clause (e); a cell no access reaches is disclosed by name.*
