C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\fbctrlportkill_20260924\panels\panel_20260924_115517\codex.txt:8629:GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\pcc2c040kill\r535_20260918\fable5_lastseat.md:12: - D (latch bit C040->MASK_LEN): correctly FILED, not a floor breach, because the (d) DEPENDS-ON bound draws operand swaps only from fields the guarded BODY reads, and MASK_LEN is not one. The `c040 predirty` note was rightly narrowed L4 (it had claimed "a DIFFERENT warned bit" generically while pinning ONE, GENCTL_LEN).
